This code retrieves the radial wind velocity using the double-edge direct-detection technique and the aerosol backscatter ratio and backscatter coefficient using the HSRL technique at 780 nm. DWLandHSRLMain loads one day of MCS netCDF data and HRRR model data, corrects for afterpulsing and detector dead time, integrates the counts in range and time, models the atmospheric temperature, pressure, and Cabannes spectrum, and performs the HSRL and wind retrievals. Uncertainties are estimated with Poisson thinning, and both products are masked by their uncertainties and plotted. Requires MATLAB, the MATLAB Parallel Computing Toolbox, and the crameri colormaps for plotting.

User-adjustable settings (date, integration time and range, pulse and delay timing, detector dead time, minimum range, background height, number of bootstrap iterations, and the calibration filenames) are in the %% 0. Pre-code section at the top of the script. File paths are set in define_paths.m, and site-specific constants (elevation, gravitational acceleration, and laser wavelength) are set in define_constants.m. The plotting section and colormap directory will also need to be changed. The retrieval assumes the lidar points vertically, so range is treated as height above the site. There is no bias correction applied in this code.

The retrieval requires the afterpulsing file from the afterpulsing code, the receiver transmission curves and HSRL calibration tables from the calibration code, and the PCA file from the Cabannes spectra training set code. The retrieval and the HSRL calibration should use the same PCA file. Two functions share the name CreateCabannesSpectrum: the one in ModelAtmosphere is used by the retrieval, and the one in CalibrationConstantCode is used by the HSRL calibration script. Each script changes into the folder containing the correct version before calling it, so do not add the full repository to the MATLAB path with addpath(genpath(...)).
